Main tasks:

Stage 1: Baseline
- Check git status.
- Read current Cisco and Build Verification reports.
- Save baseline to artifacts/codex-runs/cisco-network-foundation-baseline.md.

Stage 2: Cisco privilege diagnosis
- Auto-discover console adapter.
- Try common baud rates.
- Reach prompt.
- Attempt enable escalation using env credentials without printing secrets.
- Record:
  - initial prompt state
  - enable command sent yes/no
  - password prompt seen yes/no
  - final prompt state
  - privilege level if readable
- If privileged exec fails, improve password recovery guidance/reporting.
- Save report:
  artifacts/codex-runs/cisco-privilege-diagnosis-report.md.

Stage 3: Cisco password recovery workflow support
If privileged exec is blocked because enable password is lost:
- Add or improve a Cisco password recovery runbook/workflow page.
- Add UI next action: “Recover Cisco password from console.”
- Add detection/report text for:
  - user exec only
  - enable password rejected
  - setup wizard
  - ROMMON/bootloader prompt
  - password recovery ready
- Do not fake privileged exec.
- Save report:
  artifacts/codex-runs/cisco-password-recovery-guidance-report.md.

Stage 4: Cisco bootstrap apply if privilege works
If privileged exec succeeds:
- Apply Cisco bootstrap from .env.local.real-lab.
- Use Cisco management IP 192.168.1.204.
- Configure management VLAN/interface, gateway, local admin, enable secret, SSH v2, SCP readiness if supported, VTY login, console login, LLDP.
- Save config.
- Reload only if needed.
- Validate ping/SSH/SCP to 192.168.1.204.
- Save report:
  artifacts/codex-runs/cisco-bootstrap-apply-report.md.

Stage 5: ESXi management readiness
- Validate whether ESXi is reachable at 192.168.1.203.
- Classify ESXi API/SSH as:
  - installed and reachable
  - installer/boot state only
  - not configured yet
  - blocked by Cisco/network
- Save report:
  artifacts/codex-runs/esxi-management-readiness-report.md.

Stage 6: Build Verification
- Run provider-lab-build-verification.
- Build Verification may exit nonzero, but reports must clearly classify blockers.
- Cisco SSH/SCP should only fail hard if Cisco bootstrap was applied and still unreachable.
- ESXi API/SSH should distinguish not-installed/not-configured from actual failure.
- NetApp should remain not_configured_yet unless configured.
- Save report:
  artifacts/codex-runs/network-foundation-build-verification-report.md.

Stage 7: UI and tests
- Update Provider Status / Lab Builder UI so Cisco’s next action is obvious.
- Update Product Verification panel with staged blockers.
- Run backend tests.
- Run frontend build.
- Save final report:
  artifacts/codex-runs/cisco-network-foundation-final-report.md.

Do not print secrets.
Do not use mock results as substitutes for real lab results.
Keep going until timeout or a real blocker.
